---
/*
 * EntraSignInFieldExplorer.astro
 *
 * Purpose:
 * Helps administrators choose the Microsoft Entra sign-in log fields
 * that best answer a specific investigation question.
 *
 * The component follows the article's WHO → HOW → WHERE → WHAT → WHY →
 * RESULT → CORRELATE model and is intended as a field-selection aid,
 * not a replacement for the actual sign-in event.
 *
 * Self-contained Astro component.
 */
---

<section
  class="esfe"
  data-esfe
  aria-labelledby="esfe-title"
>
  <div class="esfe__header">
    <div class="esfe__header-copy">
      <p class="esfe__eyebrow">Field explorer</p>

      <h3 id="esfe-title">
        Which sign-in fields should you check?
      </h3>

      <p class="esfe__intro">
        Choose the question you are trying to answer. The explorer points you
        to the fields worth reviewing first and explains what those fields can
        tell you.
      </p>
    </div>

    <span class="esfe__badge" data-badge aria-live="polite">
      Choose a question
    </span>
  </div>

  <fieldset class="esfe__choices">
    <legend class="esfe__legend">
      Select the investigation question
    </legend>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="identity"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>Who attempted the sign-in?</strong>
        <span>
          Identify the actor and determine what type of identity was involved.
        </span>
        <small>WHO · Identity</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="authentication"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>How was the user authenticated?</strong>
        <span>
          Understand the client, protocol, authentication requirement, and
          individual authentication steps.
        </span>
        <small>HOW · Authentication</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="context"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>What device and location were involved?</strong>
        <span>
          Check the evaluated device state and the network context associated
          with the request.
        </span>
        <small>WHERE · Device + Location</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="resource"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>What was the identity trying to access?</strong>
        <span>
          Separate the client application from the application or resource
          being accessed.
        </span>
        <small>WHAT · Application + Resource</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="decision"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>Why was access allowed or blocked?</strong>
        <span>
          Trace Conditional Access policy evaluation and any risk signals that
          influenced the decision.
        </span>
        <small>WHY · Conditional Access + Risk</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="result"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>What was the final outcome?</strong>
        <span>
          Establish whether the sign-in succeeded or failed and why.
        </span>
        <small>RESULT · Status + Error</small>
      </span>
    </label>

    <label class="esfe__choice">
      <input
        type="radio"
        name="entra-signin-question"
        value="correlate"
      />
      <span class="esfe__marker" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></span>

      <span class="esfe__choice-body">
        <strong>How do I connect this event to related activity?</strong>
        <span>
          Use event identifiers to correlate related requests and support
          escalation.
        </span>
        <small>CORRELATE · Correlation ID + Request ID</small>
      </span>
    </label>
  </fieldset>

  <div
    class="esfe__result"
    aria-live="polite"
    aria-atomic="true"
  >
    <div class="esfe__result-head">
      <div>
        <span class="esfe__result-kicker">Start here</span>
        <h4 data-title>Select a question above.</h4>
      </div>

      <span class="esfe__result-level" data-level>
        Waiting for selection
      </span>
    </div>

    <p class="esfe__result-description" data-description>
      The right fields depend on the question you are trying to answer.
    </p>

    <div class="esfe__grid">
      <div class="esfe__card">
        <span class="esfe__card-label">Fields to inspect</span>
        <strong data-fields>
          Choose an investigation question
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="esfe__card">
        <span class="esfe__card-label">What they can tell you</span>
        <strong data-tells>
          Select a question to see the relevant evidence.
        </strong>
      </div>

      <div class="esfe__card">
        <span class="esfe__card-label">Investigation tip</span>
        <strong data-tip>
          Do not diagnose the incident from a single field.
        </strong>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="esfe__principle">
    <span class="esfe__principle-mark" aria-hidden="true">→</span>

    <p>
      <strong>Question first, fields second.</strong>
      Use the log fields that answer the investigation question, then connect
      them with the rest of the event before drawing a conclusion.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  const root = document.querySelector("[data-esfe]");

  if (root) {
    const badge = root.querySelector("[data-badge]");
    const title = root.querySelector("[data-title]");
    const level = root.querySelector("[data-level]");
    const description = root.querySelector("[data-description]");
    const fields = root.querySelector("[data-fields]");
    const tells = root.querySelector("[data-tells]");
    const tip = root.querySelector("[data-tip]");

    const results = {
      identity: {
        badge: "WHO · Identity",
        level: "Identify the actor",
        title: "Establish who attempted the sign-in.",
        description:
          "Start with the identity details before interpreting the rest of the event.",
        fields:
          "User / User Principal Name, User Type, Service Principal Name, Object ID, Sign-in Identifier",
        tells:
          "Who or what workload initiated the request and what type of identity was used.",
        tip:
          "Compare the identity with the expected account and the rest of the event context."
      },

      authentication: {
        badge: "HOW · Authentication",
        level: "Trace authentication",
        title: "Understand how the request was authenticated.",
        description:
          "Client, protocol, requirement, and authentication details together explain the authentication path.",
        fields:
          "Client app, Authentication protocol, Authentication requirement, Authentication details",
        tells:
          "Which client and protocol were used, which authentication requirement applied, and what happened during each step.",
        tip:
          "Do not stop at 'MFA required'; inspect the actual authentication details."
      },

      context: {
        badge: "WHERE · Context",
        level: "Check device and location",
        title: "Establish the device and network context.",
        description:
          "Use Device information and Location to understand what Microsoft Entra evaluated around the request.",
        fields:
          "Device ID, Device Display Name, Operating System, Browser, Compliance, Managed state, Trust Type, IP address, Location",
        tells:
          "What device and network context accompanied the request and whether those signals match expectations.",
        tip:
          "A blank device field or unfamiliar location is a signal to investigate, not a complete diagnosis."
      },

      resource: {
        badge: "WHAT · Resource",
        level: "Identify the target",
        title: "Separate the client from what the identity was actually accessing.",
        description:
          "The application initiating the flow and the underlying resource are not always the same.",
        fields:
          "Application, Application ID, Resource, Resource ID, Resource Tenant, Resource Service Principal",
        tells:
          "Which application and resource were involved in the access attempt.",
        tip:
          "Use Resource to isolate app-specific problems and service dependencies."
      },

      decision: {
        badge: "WHY · Access decision",
        level: "Explain the decision",
        title: "Find out why policy allowed, restricted, or blocked the request.",
        description:
          "Conditional Access and risk information explain the policy side of the access decision.",
        fields:
          "Conditional Access, Policy Result, Failure Reason, Requirement, Grant Controls, Report-only Result, Risk",
        tells:
          "Which policies applied, which requirements were introduced, and whether risk signals influenced the outcome.",
        tip:
          "One policy showing Success does not prove that the overall sign-in succeeded."
      },

      result: {
        badge: "RESULT · Outcome",
        level: "Confirm the outcome",
        title: "Establish exactly what happened to the sign-in.",
        description:
          "Status and error information tell you the result and provide the first clue for deeper investigation.",
        fields:
          "Status, Error Code, Failure Reason, Additional Details",
        tells:
          "Whether the request succeeded or failed and the available explanation for that result.",
        tip:
          "Treat Status as the start of the investigation, not the end."
      },

      correlate: {
        badge: "CORRELATE · Connect",
        level: "Link related events",
        title: "Connect the event to related activity.",
        description:
          "Correlation and request identifiers help you find related events or provide useful information during escalation.",
        fields:
          "Correlation ID, Request ID, Session ID, Original Request ID, Date / Time (UTC)",
        tells:
          "Which other events or requests may belong to the same investigation or token flow.",
        tip:
          "Retain correlation information when escalating an authentication issue."
      }
    };

    root
      .querySelectorAll('input[name="entra-signin-question"]')
      .forEach((input) => {
        input.addEventListener("change", (event) => {
          const value = event.currentTarget.value;
          const result = results[value];

          if (!result) return;

          root.dataset.state = value;
          badge.textContent = result.badge;
          level.textContent = result.level;
          title.textContent = result.title;
          description.textContent = result.description;
          fields.textContent = result.fields;
          tells.textContent = result.tells;
          tip.textContent = result.tip;
        });
      });
  }
</script>

<style>
  .esfe {
    --esfe-surface: var(--surface-primary, #ffffff);
    --esfe-surface-soft: var(--surface-secondary, #f8fafc);
    --esfe-text: var(--text-primary, #0f172a);
    --esfe-text-secondary: var(--text-secondary, #475569);
    --esfe-text-tertiary: var(--text-tertiary, #64748b);
    --esfe-border: var(--border-default, #dbe3ec);
    --esfe-border-soft: var(--border-subtle, #e7edf4);
    --esfe-accent: var(--color-accent, #4ea1e0);
    --esfe-state: var(--esfe-accent);

    width: 100%;
    margin-block: var(--space-10, 2.5rem);
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 3vw, 2rem);
    color: var(--esfe-text);
    background: var(--esfe-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--esfe-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-lg, 0.875rem);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .esfe[data-state="identity"] { --esfe-state: #2563eb; }
  .esfe[data-state="authentication"] { --esfe-state: #6d3bb8; }
  .esfe[data-state="context"] { --esfe-state: #15803d; }
  .esfe[data-state="resource"] { --esfe-state: #0f8a8a; }
  .esfe[data-state="decision"] { --esfe-state: #c2410c; }
  .esfe[data-state="result"] { --esfe-state: #dc2626; }
  .esfe[data-state="correlate"] { --esfe-state: #1d4ed8; }

  .esfe__header {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
  }

  .esfe__eyebrow {
    margin: 0 0 0.25rem;
    color: var(--esfe-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .esfe h3,
  .esfe h4,
  .esfe p {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .esfe h3 {
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 2vw, 1.6rem);
    line-height: 1.2;
  }

  .esfe__intro {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--esfe-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .esfe__badge {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    align-self: flex-start;
    padding: 0.45rem 0.75rem;
    color: var(--esfe-state);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--esfe-state) 8%, var(--esfe-surface));
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--esfe-state) 30%, var(--esfe-border));
    border-radius: 999px;
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    text-align: center;
  }

  .esfe__choices {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
  }

  .esfe__legend {
    width: 100%;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--esfe-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .esfe__choice {
    position: relative;
    display: block;
    height: 100%;
    padding: 0.95rem;
    background: var(--esfe-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--esfe-border);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
    cursor: pointer;
    transition:
      border-color 160ms ease,
      background-color 160ms ease,
      box-shadow 160ms ease,
      transform 160ms ease;
  }

  .esfe__choice:hover {
    transform: translateY(-1px);
    border-color: var(--esfe-accent);
    box-shadow: var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .esfe__choice:has(input:focus-visible) {
    outline: 2px solid var(--esfe-accent);
    outline-offset: 2px;
  }

  .esfe__choice input {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    opacity: 0;
    pointer-events: none;
  }

  .esfe__choice:has(input:checked) {
    border-color: var(--esfe-state);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--esfe-state) 8%, var(--esfe-surface));
    box-shadow:
      inset 0 0 0 1px var(--esfe-state),
      var(--shadow-sm, 0 1px 2px rgb(15 23 42 / 0.06));
  }

  .esfe__marker {
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    width: 1.15rem;
    height: 1.15rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    border: 2px solid var(--esfe-text-tertiary);
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .esfe__marker span {
    width: 0.48rem;
    height: 0.48rem;
    border-radius: 50%;
  }

  .esfe__choice:has(input:checked) .esfe__marker {
    border-color: var(--esfe-state);
  }

  .esfe__choice:has(input:checked) .esfe__marker span {
    background: var(--esfe-state);
  }

  .esfe__choice-body {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
  }

  .esfe__choice-body strong {
    color: var(--esfe-text);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .esfe__choice-body > span {
    color: var(--esfe-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.5;
  }

  .esfe__choice-body small {
    color: var(--esfe-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }

  .esfe__result {
    margin-top: var(--space-6, 1.5rem);
    padding: 1.2rem;
    background: var(--esfe-surface-soft);
    border: 1px solid var(--esfe-border);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--esfe-state);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .esfe__result-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 1rem;
  }

  .esfe__result-kicker {
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
    color: var(--esfe-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .esfe__result h4 {
    margin-bottom: 0;
    color: var(--esfe-text);
    font-size: var(--font-size-lg, 1.1rem);
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .esfe__result-level {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--esfe-state);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .esfe__result-description {
    max-width: 72ch;
    margin: 0.65rem 0 0;
    color: var(--esfe-text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }

  .esfe__grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
    gap: var(--space-3, 0.75rem);
    margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .esfe__card {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.35rem;
    padding: 0.9rem;
    background: var(--esfe-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--esfe-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-sm, 0.5rem);
  }

  .esfe__card-label {
    color: var(--esfe-text-tertiary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-xs, 0.75rem);
    font-weight: 700;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .esfe__card strong {
    color: var(--esfe-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  .esfe__principle {
    display: flex;
    align-items: flex-start;
    gap: 0.75rem;
    margin-top: 1rem;
    padding: 0.9rem 1rem;
    background: var(--esfe-surface);
    border: 1px solid var(--esfe-border-soft);
    border-radius: var(--radius-md, 0.65rem);
  }

  .esfe__principle-mark {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    color: var(--esfe-accent);
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .esfe__principle p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--esfe-text-secondary);
    font-size: var(--font-size-sm, 0.875rem);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }

  @media (max-width: 800px) {
    .esfe__choices {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }

    .esfe__grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .esfe {
      padding: 1rem;
    }

    .esfe__header {
      display: grid;
      gap: 0.9rem;
    }

    .esfe__badge {
      justify-self: start;
    }

    .esfe__result-head {
      align-items: flex-start;
      flex-direction: column;
      gap: 0.35rem;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .esfe__choice {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
</style>
